y TCP -> pacotes MU | | | +-- CRIPTO: Layer-1, XorData, GetGameServerKeys | | | +-- TCP proprio (44413, log de pacotes + SEND) | | | +-- name rewrite (HexDL) | | | +-- INJECAO: InjectToServer/C1Attack/SkillC1 + fila skill | | | | | +-- MonsterTracker AttackModule (+~400 linhas de debug RE) | | +-- SkillHook SimpleModulusCipher ViewportMap SkillMap | | +-- GameMemory (40 getters inline em 1 namespace flat) | +-------------------------------------------------------------------------+ MORTOS (nao estao no build, so ocupam espaco): PsBypass.cpp DllNotifyHook.cpp MainPatcher.cpp PsPacketHook.cpp StartupHook.cpp AsyncScanner.cpp VPTracer.cpp <- familia PS.dll PacketSniffer.cpp.new <- rascunho ``` ## Descobertas que ajustam o plano anterior 1. **Dois canais TCP, não um** — dúvida da Fase 2 resolvida: `TcpClient` (44412) é o canal de **comandos** (CMD ATTACK...), e o socket do PacketSniffer (44413) é o canal de **pacotes** (log PKT + SEND). Não há overlap …\n- **Tools:** list_directory, glob, ask_user, run_command, read_file, search_files","vector":[0.029220654,0.05140201,-0.16488543,-0.016935844,0.082637966,-0.08790688,0.018695446,0.011508713,-0.0628072,-0.044516016,-0.038928203,0.02157775,0.05722319,-0.022112822,0.00033445205,-0.049718738,-0.031558108,-0.01758117,-0.06994791,0.017993722,0.0028603699,-0.012830948,-0.022741579,0.0144497715,0.09169462,0.04241376,-0.007951301,0.020670079,-0.043784298,-0.016079195,0.06843503,-0.009161888,-0.02677047,-0.012393035,-0.035822,-0.060683962,0.044892274,-0.011645806,0.00095840293,0.021494478,-0.007115764,-0.038796984,-0.02407068,-0.0330012,0.041762576,0.032940045,0.07962157,-0.0069482233,0.06899432,-0.11762551,0.01099617,0.04378732,0.008777513,-0.06474644,0.054785624,0.00646029,-0.022269985,0.009799392,0.0424006,-0.039999902,0.06548988,0.07076686,0.027812675,0.07588522,0.0462836,-0.008614923,-0.08255582,0.024657294,-0.010810288,-0.003448924,0.047905646,-0.007956134,0.0019597292,-0.0024734666,0.020705605,0.043765675,-0.019614967,-0.02